{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact ab74034699b01adceb570e2ed96a4786f9cc51a9 (tree 7d394386ab9d06a1f01b2c67fa944997b4fd23fb), both artifacts examined with 848f9310 primary. This is a design review, not implementation, gate, native or deployment acceptance.\n\nArchitecture: the fixed generic tools, definition-driven descriptions and native judge are a useful direction. Claim (a) is not yet established: the advertised act interface omits existing native inputs. Claim (c) needs a total declaration contract and an unfamiliar-application witness, not only an import prohibition and two familiar examples. Preserve the complete scope while correcting these gaps.\n\nSecurity: changes needed for caller-known operation identity, exact requested meaning and atomic custody, intentional credential delivery, honest diagnostic attribution and the loopback signing boundary. Discovery is information, not authority; keep the native scope as judge.\n\nSimplification: ten tools and immutable definitions can reduce per-application code. Do not meet byte or call budgets by omitting valid acts, guard forms, values or recovery. W1-W7 are proposed acceptance witnesses; their being future work is appropriate for a design, but the current interfaces and accounting must make them possible.\n\nRequired corrections:\n\n1. [P2] Cover founding and all native beside inputs (plan:103,342; contract/src/intent.ts:36; contract/src/definition.ts:81). act currently requires an existing scope and reads its summary/definition, but W2 starts by founding a room, whose native target is null. Specify the generic no-existing-scope preparation/discovery path and initial definition/seed inputs. Also specify presented facts and complete beside values/texts, including exact domain/digest binding and retained replay. An act's fields do not replace its presents. W1 and W2 must exercise these existing native forms without app-specific branches.\n\n2. [P2] Reconcile authorized Git credential delivery with the blanket output prohibition (plan:131-134,237-239,345). clone/propose requires text of the read credential, while W4 forbids that credential in every tool output. Define an intentional, narrowly authorized credential channel or an opaque handle consumed by a generic local Git helper. Keep it out of unrelated reads, errors, histories, logs and other actors/scopes. Witness both the useful Git composition and the confidentiality boundary; redacting everything while claiming clone complete is insufficient.\n\n3. [P2] Render only diagnostics returned by the judge (plan:225-227; contract/src/result.ts:67-71). Native refused answers contain reason, optional name and judgedAt, but no failed-guard ordinal or offending field/item. Two unnamed guards can produce indistinguishable guard-failed answers; the transport cannot state guard 3 of 3. Use an explicitly unattributed fallback with possible constraints, and do not re-judge a later summary to invent the earlier failed predicate. Apply this limit to field/item categories too. W4 should include multiple unnamed guards and state moving after judgment. A diagnostic protocol extension would be a separate decision, not this note's no-protocol-change implementation.\n\n4. [P2] Keep required caller keys and define custody semantics (plan:103,296-306). Effective adopted decision 775acdd32aa33ac52bde54c74d925ea633881634 explicitly requires idempotencyKey on MCP act tools. Optional generated keys conflict with that decision and are unknowable after the first MCP reply is lost. Require a caller-known key before dispatch. Distinguish first preparation from missing earlier custody; retain/read back exact envelope and beside inputs atomically under exclusive coordination across processes sharing storage. Bind records to service/tenant, signer, scope/incarnation and requested meaning. Same-key/different-kind/on/fields/inputs must refuse without resending old meaning. Settle remains read-only; recovery must not sign afresh. Preserve unresolved records and recorded terminal outcomes at capacity. W6 needs first MCP reply loss, conflicting concurrent first use, changed meaning, restart and full-store recovery, not only a lost scope reply with a known key.\n\n5. [P2] Make declaration rendering total (plan:165-183; contract/src/definition.ts:133-153,189-191). The table omits distinct/sameSet guards and presented/element/part operands. Specify every supported native form and nesting/binding semantics, with complete machine-readable declarations reachable after bounded prose. Add a valid unfamiliar declared application and non-repository scope to W1/W2, including standing/activation changes. The deferred Counting join example is not yet a worked readability example; give its actual derived wording or label it explicitly as future evidence. Do not silently discard predicates to meet sentence bounds.\n\n6. [P2] Define end-to-end bounds that preserve complete output (plan:319-334). act can already consume three reads and then promises child-scope readbacks; that exceeds its three-read ceiling before session acquisition/renewal or signed-read fallback. Either include these in the measured boundary or reserve child discovery for wait. Measure full client-visible MCP responses, including structuredContent/envelopes, not text alone. Provide byte-bounded continuation or large-value handling for arbitrary valid definitions, items, entries and retained inputs; native bounds allow 64 acts/256 KiB definitions, 256 KiB entries and 1 MiB inputs. Include cold/warm/expired/refused-session, created children, pagination, standing/activation refresh and long-lived custody lifecycle witnesses. The append-only 256-record store otherwise stops a continuous agent after 256 settled acts; define safe terminal archival/rotation while preserving unknown custody and old-key replay rules. These are design requirements, not a demand to run implementation tests before design approval.\n\n7. [P2] Correct generic act annotations and local HTTP boundaries (plan:103,272-274,351). A generic act can change or remove declared state; it cannot universally advertise not destructive. Repeat calls with fresh generated keys also cannot universally be idempotent. Use conservative, truthful annotations consistent with required-key semantics. Host validation and loopback binding do not replace Origin validation: a browser request to the loopback address has a valid local Host. Specify rejection of untrusted Origin and appropriate local-client authentication, with W7 witnesses, plus actor/session/custody separation for hosted bearer changes. Official MCP transport requirements and SDK Origin validation documentation support this boundary:\nhttps://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports\nhttps://ts.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/v2/api/@modelcontextprotocol/server/server/middleware/originValidation.html\n\n8. [P2] Complete the retained/replaced/outstanding matrix (plan:35-50,358-370). Read effective775 and the full revision-4 note and Plan009, then explicitly account for their still-valid outcomes: required keys, advertised output schemas/annotations, OAuth stage2 before finals with consent/client/redirect/audience/current-authority/revocation boundaries, and the useful library/resource/prompt/Tasks/MCP Apps/reviewer-without-checkout/named-client acceptance outcomes. Current one-service direction legitimately replaces obsolete application-server topology and lane vocabulary; map those to scope-model successors or cite a deliberate replacement decision. Preserve later outcomes as separately owned work, without making all later stages prerequisites for the local implementation. Byte budgets versus earlier token gates are a proposed policy change to account for, not an implicitly retired gate. Also correct nine tools in the kept table to ten.\n\nCoverage and evidence: Root FULL-read Plan031 BODY (28,829B; SHA5f298ed4), all four peer final analyses/audits, effective775 statement/decision, and the new README index entry/context plus complete U3. Peer FULL BODY/U3/native-contract coverage and full old note/Plan009 were independently matched to native bytes, hashes, LF, contiguous spans and EOF. README's unchanged 715,460B whole body is not claimed FULL-read or blanket-approved. The exact parent is d309b6b9; only Plan031 and the eleven-line index insertion change, with 1,398 unaffected parent leaves preserved. Audits: mcp031-ab740-native-peer-audit.json SHA5cd6712bfb2dacd43cc519cc6bdb083abc9ebca159f5439d110c136f18fa4bd2; mcp031-ab740-adoption-inheritance-audit.json SHA01199983201d0e670d21307b2b594f6c20c49ab2413d6a0124753472c1c38a17. No Source execution, tests, gate, install, private program/log/credential reads, browser or provider action by checker. Normal prepare binds only design request2c3832/promise059afc; no cloud implementation or broader original MCP scope closes through this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:848f931087728e82d08ee5e90b4a17737fceaff0","binding":"assigned","head":"ab74034699b01adceb570e2ed96a4786f9cc51a9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bb78993ad54dcf0f20f132512b872d6b42081f92\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:059afc6810129b357bbab51774fc34657da45ac5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:beb2bf650457bc56ca45626ecdc7857ce8b429d7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}